-- Rules that start themselves again with no time passing, beside the same
-- rules with a deadline one day later, which L4 checks come to an end. Recursion-limit
-- ruling L3 (2026-11-20) asks for a positive and a
-- negative fixture for each shape a warning fires on, and ruling L4 says that
-- @ends-because does not silence this warning. Both are described in
-- doc/reference/regulative/rules-that-start-themselves-again.md, and the
-- golden pins the text of each message.

DECLARE Person IS ONE OF Alex, Sam
DECLARE Action IS ONE OF `pay rent`

-- Warns: WITHIN 0, so the time of each copy is up the moment it starts.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`pay at once` MEANS
    PARTY Alex
    MUST `pay rent`
    WITHIN 0
    LEST `pay at once`

-- No warning: WITHIN 1, so each copy waits a day before the next one starts.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`pay within a day` MEANS
    PARTY Alex
    MUST `pay rent`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST `pay within a day`

-- Warns, for a permission too, and the mark above it does not silence it.
@ends-because Alex always takes the chance
GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`chance at once` MEANS
    PARTY Alex
    MAY `pay rent`
    WITHIN 0
    LEST `chance at once`
